 "final_text": "## Answer\n\n**Parent's books (Contoso USMF, ERP intercompany AR account IC\u2011001 \"CES Direct LLC\"):** 3 open invoices totaling **$76,500**\n- ICINV\u201101 \u2014 Shared services allocation Q4 \u2014 $30,000 (posted 2026\u201101\u201110)\n- ICINV\u201102 \u2014 Inventory transfer January \u2014 $24,000 (posted 2026\u201102\u201105)\n- ICINV\u201103 \u2014 February management fee \u2014 $22,500 (posted 2026\u201102\u201127)\n\n**CES Direct's own books (their intercompany payable schedule, as of 2026\u201102\u201128):** **$54,000**\n- ICINV\u201101 \u2014 $30,000 (booked)\n- ICINV\u201102 \u2014 $24,000 (booked)\n\n**Difference: $22,500** \u2014 exactly ICINV\u201103, the February management fee. The parent invoiced it on 2/27, one day before CES Direct's close, and CES Direct hadn't yet recorded it in their books. It's a month-end cutoff/timing gap, not a pricing dispute \u2014 the other two invoices tie out perfectly between both sets of books.\n\nSubmitted via `submit_answer`.",
